<h3>Recap of the previous basics course</h3>
<ul>
    <li>AI tools come not only as the web but also as a <strong>desktop app and a terminal (Claude Code)</strong>.</li>
    <li>Terminal basics &mdash; <code>pwd</code> · <code>cd</code> · <code>mkdir</code>, and running <code>claude</code> in a folder.</li>
    <li>Research → file → building a website, and applying design with the <strong>design system skill</strong>.</li>
    <li>Creating an <strong>agent</strong> to analyze papers, and <strong>parallel processing</strong> with multiple agents.</li>
    <li>The <strong>importance of context</strong> when working with AI, and managing token usage.</li>
</ul>

<h3>About the instructor — FDE</h3>
<p>The instructor belongs to Kakao's <strong>FDE (Forward Deployed Engineer)</strong> organization. FDE is a role that started with Palantir and is now widely hired at OpenAI · Anthropic as well; FDEs are deployed on site at a client (or an internal organization), <strong>rapidly build</strong> the systems needed <strong>with AI</strong>, and help with AX (AI transformation) training and adoption.</p>

